 \section{Agreement and Disagreement With Previous Research}
-Evidence from welding itself qualifies the expectation of a fusion advantage. In one penetration-state study, the clean image-only, audio-only, and fused models each reached 100\% accuracy \citep[Tables~1--3]{Hua2026Weld}. Distinct physical measurements may be available even when the reported endpoint leaves no measurable room for a clean gain. In the published HANDOVER study, five-class outcome accuracy averaged over five trainings was 69.1\% with video and force/torque and 67.9\% after gripper state was added \citep[Table~III]{Thoduka2024Handover}. The present HANDOVER implementation uses binary outcomes, different models, and failure AP. The common finding is that an additional stream can lower performance on a shared outcome. Absolute scores from the two experiments answer different questions.
+Pretrained spatial features are reasonable candidates because PatchCore demonstrates useful industrial inspection from intermediate CNN features, while RT-DETR learns a multiscale hierarchy for detection \citep{Roth2022Towards,Zhao2024RTDETR}. Their positive findings do not imply that every downstream component helps. The matched REASSEMBLE spatial-encoder comparison favored CNN-based F2 over the hybrid representation by .0158 AP (95\% CI [.0058, .0248]). Different feature widths and head sizes prevent attribution solely to attention. This limits transfer of the detector's architectural conclusions to action outcomes; it does not contradict its detection benchmark.
+
+PatchTST's favorable forecasting ablation supports local patch tokens and channel-shared temporal encoding \citep{Nie2023PatchTST}. Our longer-budget result confirms that optimization duration affected the scratch classifier, yet statistics remained stronger. Their successful same-sensor combination supports complementary predictive use rather than replacement by the higher-scoring representation. Classical geometry's competitiveness in inspection is consistent with taking compact, task-relevant summaries seriously \citep{Horwitz2023Back}; it does not establish why these particular robot statistics work. Likewise, TimeSformer's divided spatial--temporal attention motivates examining temporal organization \citep{P034}. The boundary-pooling gain supports sensitivity to aggregation, but uses an order-invariant mean within a selected interval and does not test that learned-attention mechanism.
 
-Other industrial studies report clear gains within their respective protocols. Acoustic--thermal gearbox monitoring achieved 99.54\% mean accuracy against 90.54\% for the stronger individual thermal stream on a random within-condition split \citep[Table~2]{Ying2025Trustworthy}. On MVTec~3D-AD, combining RGB and 3D inputs raised mean image AUROC to 93.7\% from 88.0\% for RGB alone \citep[Table~3]{Rudolph2023Asymmetric}. These results concern different acquisition regimes and outcomes from completed-action failure. Conversely, studies of multimodal optimization and industrial input subsets identify losses against stronger individual channels \citep{Wang2020What,Horwitz2023Back,Goodarzi2023Deep}. REASSEMBLE and the external studies provide evidence in both directions. The performance differences alone cannot identify whether limited visibility, an unsuitable representation, or the fusion training procedure caused a particular loss.
+The positive REASSEMBLE F2 contrast and negative external contrasts agree with a conditional view of fusion. Welding's image-only, audio-only and fused penetration classifiers all reached 100\% clean accuracy \citep[Tables~1--3]{Hua2026Weld}. Published HANDOVER five-class accuracy fell from 69.1\% with video and force/torque to 67.9\% after adding gripper state \citep[Table~III]{Thoduka2024Handover}; our binary, differently fitted AP comparison is not a replication. Other settings do show gains: acoustic--thermal gearbox monitoring reports 99.54\% against 90.54\% for thermal alone under a random within-condition split \citep[Table~2]{Ying2025Trustworthy}. Such results disagree with an unconditional prediction of a gain here, not with the bounded negative findings in MSM or ViFailback. Wang and colleagues identify unequal overfitting and optimization difficulties in jointly trained multimodal networks \citep{Wang2020What}. They supply plausible competing mechanisms, not a demonstrated cause of losses in our separately fitted branches and stacker.
 
-Previous work provides both a theory and experimental tests of quality-aware weighting \citep{Zhang2023QMF}. RGB--geometry research tests absent 3D input \citep[Table~3]{P026}, and fuzzy-regularized camera--telemetry fusion tests corruption in simulated robot pose regression \citep{Altinses2023Fuzzy}. Training-time removal of images, a model designed for single-stream inference, an unannounced sensor malfunction, and adaptation with target-domain data impose different information constraints. The remaining question for a particular industrial task is whether a quality signal changes decisions beneficially once the static and unimodal controls have comparable observations, calibration, and training exposure.
+Stacking's use of cross-validated probability outputs motivates a small learned combiner \citep{Ting1999Issues}. Our within-fold audit establishes beneficial visual ordering changes in the saved F2, while its pooled advantage over averaging remains unresolved. This distinguishes complementary predictions from evidence that learning the combiner is necessary. It also explains why the coefficients cannot be read as causal modality percentages.
+
+Adaptive weighting has a positive precedent: QMF links useful uncertainty weighting to a generalization bound and reports gains under specified RGB--depth corruption \citep{Zhang2023QMF}. Our anchored clean increment, .0210 [.0015, .0419], supports a particular context-dependent adjustment, whereas the matched-exposure robustness increment, .0097 [$-.0034$, .0228], remains unresolved. This is neither a replication nor a refutation of QMF: the quality variables, links, training procedures and targets differ. It identifies what does not transfer automatically from its result. Lower clean recall and higher ECE after anchored adjustment further show that improved AP is not calibrated reliability. This agrees with evidence that clean calibration need not survive shift \citep{P008}. Missing-input and simulated-robot studies address other access regimes \citep{P026,Altinses2023Fuzzy}; shared fallback cannot establish adaptive fault recognition.
 
